 Multiline values: $key, then the lines under it (one indent level removed). Blank lines inside are kept.
$query sql
	SELECT name, age
	FROM users

	WHERE age > 30
		AND name LIKE 'a%'


 Wide form: the rest of the line is the value, one line per entry
$cmd	pip install rp	python train.py --epochs 10

 A tag is optional, and a shebang inside the block is just text
$script
	#!/bin/bash
	echo "hello world"

 Comma keys, and an empty block
$a,b
	shared
$empty
after 1

 Nested: blocks work at any depth, and a tab inside a block line is kept
config	db	$init
		CREATE TABLE t (
			id	INT
		);
config	db	port 5432
